course: dictionary
lesson: 12557
title: Devoted: loyal, or given to something
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Mia is a devoted friend. She visits Sam every day and never forgets his birthday.» The clues are visits every day and never forgets. Devoted means very loving and loyal.
explain: Devoted can also mean giving a lot of time and energy to something. «Ravi is devoted to his piano practice.» He spends lots of time on the piano, so devoted to means giving a lot of time to something.
explain: Books use devoted in another way. «The last page is devoted to animals.» Here devoted means the page gives its time and space to animals. Try the swap test: the page is given to animals. It still makes sense.
fact: «Devoted» is an adjective. It means very loving and loyal, as in «a devoted dog».
fact: «Devoted to» means giving a lot of time and energy to something, as in «devoted to music».
fact: «Devoted» is also the past form of the verb devote, which means to give time or space to something. «The page is devoted to animals» means the page is given over to animals.
fact: Keep the phrase together: you say devoted to something, and the word after to names the thing.
exercise: «The little puppy waited at the door for his devoted owner.» What does devoted mean? | Lost and cold | *Very loving and loyal | Angry at everyone | Very tired
exercise: «Ali is devoted to his science club.» What does devoted to mean here? | Bored of something | Far away from something | *Giving lots of time and energy to something | Afraid of something
exercise: «Chapter three is devoted to volcanoes.» What does this tell you? | The chapter has been torn out | *The chapter gives its time and space to volcanoes | Chapter three has lost its pages | The chapter is about the sea
test: «Her dog is devoted to her and follows her everywhere.» What does devoted mean? | Very cold | *Very loving and loyal | Very hungry | Very fast
test: «Hours were devoted to practice before the match.» What does devoted mean here? | Put away in a box | *Given lots of time to something | Forgotten completely | Shouted loudly
exam: «Her dog is devoted to her.» What does devoted mean in this sentence? | Very dirty | Very sleepy | Very quick | *Very loyal and loving
